Illmari is a late-60s half-elf male, with black, slicked back hair and scars on his face. He has a raiment of the [[Iridescent Host|Host]].

Illmari is the current proprietor of the [[Sin and Tonic]] and the founder of the mercenary group [[Org/Iconoclasm/index|Iconoclasm]]. He was one of the first to capitalize on hearing the [[Voidsong]], collecting like-minded people to investigate its source and meaning.

The founder of [[Org/Iconoclasm/index|Iconoclasm]], [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Illmari Vaino|Illmari]] is better known around [[Sin and Tonic]] as a cook — a tension between those two identities that those who know him tend not to press on.

He had not come back to the bar by the night after the Concordia fight. He goes out from time to time, but usually says where he is going, and by then he had been gone long enough that Ginny was concerned. According to Ginny he left the same night the Party went to the party at Teller's Run. [[People/Argyle|Argyle]] guessed he had gone to the party alone and might feel responsible for the deaths there, but no one could find him, and Anouk, Anaïs, Ginny, Dura and Elias had nothing to add.

Belvedere dug up what could be found of his past. He was born in [[Geography/Velthara/index|Velthara]], and his family moved to [[Geography/Calaria/index|Calaria]] at some point after. He ran an adventuring company that, as adventuring was swallowed up by the orgs, tried to turn mercenary. Most of his party died in an accident around the time the [[Phenomena/Harmony/Voidsong|Voidsong]] appeared, the date uncertain by a little on either side. Only Illmari and [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Elias Ramsey|Elias]] came out of it, and they came out with treasure enough for Illmari to buy the [[Sin and Tonic]]. He then called publicly for anyone willing to look into the song, and [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Flynn|Flynn]] and one other joined him near the start, followed by [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Dura Oil-Drinker|Dura]] and others. He was never an outgoing man, and little of his private life is on record.
